{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1790854182530,"sessionID":"ses_f08c5f12affeHe8k5kbph5Qroc","part":{"id":"prt_0f73a36790018Jcz5M5FweNanb","messageID":"msg_0f73a2cc1001XidChwjwzwD54T","sessionID":"ses_f08c5f12affeHe8k5kbph5Qroc","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1790854189049,"sessionID":"ses_f08c5f12affeHe8k5kbph5Qroc","part":{"id":"prt_0f73a492b001XfILGYAPFQRkp2","messageID":"msg_0f73a2cc1001XidChwjwzwD54T","sessionID":"ses_f08c5f12affeHe8k5kbph5Qroc","type":"text","text":"The bug is in `overlaps`: it uses `<=`, which counts touching intervals (e.g., `[0,2)` and `[2,4)`) and empty intervals as overlapping. For half-open intervals the ends are exclusive, so overlap requires the later start to be strictly before the earlier end. Applying the fix:\n\n{\"action\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"intervals.py\",\"old\":\"    return max(left[0], right[0]) <= min(left[1], right[1])\",\"new\":\"    return max(left[0], right[0]) < min(left[1], right[1])\"}","time":{"start":1790854187307,"end":1790854189039}}}
